Delete Contact:
This one is also pretty self explanatory it just deletes a row in the contacts table

CREATE DEFINER=`root`@`localhost` PROCEDURE `DeleteContact`(
	IN DelFirstName VARCHAR(50),
    IN DelLastName VARCHAR(50),
    IN DelUserAttribution VARCHAR(50)

)
BEGIN
DELETE FROM Contacts WHERE FirstName = DelFirstName AND LastName = DelLastName AND UserAttribution = DelUserAttribution;

END


///////////////
search contacts:
This procedure uses the percentage sign to search for partial names so that if a person is named Noah and they type in ‘No’ the contact will show up. I might add a space in the concat first name and last name section to better match partial first name plus last name searches.

CREATE DEFINER=`root`@`localhost` PROCEDURE `ContactSearch`(
	IN SearchAttribution VARCHAR(50),
    IN SearchName VARCHAR(50)
)
BEGIN
SELECT * FROM Contacts WHERE UserAttribution = SearchAttribution AND CONCAT(FirstName,LastName)  like concat('%',SearchName,'%');
END

Sign Up:
This creates a new user, the username must be unique and the procedure will fail if its not. This is so we don't have identical users  whose contacts are mixed together.
CREATE DEFINER=`root`@`localhost` PROCEDURE `AddUser`(
	IN NewUser varchar(50),
    IN NewPassword varchar(50)

)
BEGIN
	INSERT INTO Users (Username, UserPassword)
	VALUES (NewUser,NewPassword);
END

